{%- comment -%}
  New arrivals — the product grid under the hero. Port of the arrivals block in
  app/page.tsx.

  PLACEHOLDER MODE. With no products in the collection the grid still renders,
  filled with placeholder cards at the exact card proportions — so the grid, its
  gaps and its rhythm are the real ones before the store has a catalogue. The
  moment products exist the same markup renders them; nothing here changes.

  DEVIATION — two-up on the phone. app/page.tsx:115 stacks these cards one to a
  row below `sm`; the theme runs two. The card's own type step is what settles
  it: snippets/product-card.liquid drops the name a rung to --text-h3 below `sm`
  "where the catalogue runs two cards to a row and the column is about 155px
  wide". At one-up the column is ~327px, so the card is set for a layout it is
  not in — and with no catalogue imported the section is eight full-width tone
  blocks, roughly 3,760px of identical grey between the hero and the voices
  wall. The gap set is now byte-identical to main-collection.liquid:48 so the
  card renders at the same size on the home page and in the catalogue.

  The `sizes` hint follows the grid: two-up means ~45vw on a phone, not 90vw,
  which is what lets image_tag pick the smaller candidate.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign source = collections[section.settings.collection]
  assign shown = section.settings.count
  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1024px) 23vw, 45vw'
-%}

<section aria-labelledby="arrivals-heading" class="pt-section">
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter flex flex-col gap-10">
    {%- comment -%}
      DEVIATION — left-aligned, and no rule. The design centres this heading
      over the same 64x3 pill the voices wall and the Instagram strip carry, so
      three consecutive sections opened with one identical treatment and the page
      read as a single texture. The pill was decorative and aria-hidden, so
      dropping it changes nothing a reader can name.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div data-reveal>
      <h2 id="arrivals-heading" class="text-h1 leading-h1">
        {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-4 gap-y-8 sm:gap-x-7 sm:gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {%- comment -%}
      A partially stocked collection is a THIRD fact, and neither branch used to
        handle it. The old shape was "any products at all -> render them, otherwise
        render `shown` placeholders", so a collection holding one piece drew exactly
        one tile and the rest of the rail was empty. On the marquee that also killed
        the motion: a two-tile track is narrower than the viewport, so translateX(-50%)
        had nothing to travel over and the strip sat still looking broken. It will
        happen again on the real import, which lands eleven pieces one at a time.
        So: render what exists, then top up with labelled placeholders to `shown`.
    {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign real = source.products.size -%}
      {%- if real > shown -%}{%- assign real = shown -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign pad = shown | minus: real -%}
      {%- for product in source.products limit: shown -%}
        <div data-reveal>{% render 'product-card', product: product, sizes: card_sizes %}</div>
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if pad > 0 -%}
        {%- for i in (1..pad) -%}
          <div data-reveal>{% render 'product-card', sizes: card_sizes %}</div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.cta != blank -%}
      <div data-reveal class="flex justify-center">
        <a
          href="{{ section.settings.href | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
          class="inline-flex min-h-13 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-sm border border-ink-subtle bg-transparent px-11 text-caption uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-brand transition-[background-color,color,border-color,transform] duration-(--duration-base) ease-out hover:border-brand hover:bg-brand hover:text-on-brand active:translate-y-px"
        >
          {{ section.settings.cta }}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'arrow-right', class: 'size-5' %}
        </a>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "New arrivals",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "collection", "id": "collection", "label": "Collection" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "New arrivals" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "count", "label": "Products shown", "min": 4, "max": 12, "step": 4, "default": 8 },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta", "label": "Button label", "default": "View all" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "href", "label": "Button link" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "New arrivals" }]
}
{% endschema %}
